1
00:00:01,090 --> 00:00:02,160
Mr.

2
00:00:02,160 --> 00:00:08,320
Wu is telling the students how to get along with friends.

3
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:16,190
Listen to him and complete the notes below. Hello students!

4
00:00:16,190 --> 00:00:22,220
I'm going to give you some tips on how to get along with your friends.

5
00:00:22,220 --> 00:00:25,950
First, be a good listener.

6
00:00:25,950 --> 00:00:32,320
It's important to get to know your friends well, so listen to them.

7
00:00:32,320 --> 00:00:39,650
You can ask questions to show that you're interested in what they're saying.

8
00:00:39,650 --> 00:00:44,730
Body language can also help show that you're listening.

9
00:00:44,730 --> 00:00:52,810
Try to look at your friends when they're talking, and nod your head from time to time.

10
00:00:52,810 --> 00:00:57,300
Second, be a cheerful person.

11
00:00:57,300 --> 00:01:03,410
When you're with friends, focus on the good things in life.

12
00:01:03,410 --> 00:01:08,630
Share funny stories and happy experiences with them.

13
00:01:08,630 --> 00:01:18,280
It's also good to notice and care about your friends' feelings, so you can help them if they feel bad.

14
00:01:18,280 --> 00:01:25,050
A good friend makes you happy and cheers you up when you feel down.

15
00:01:25,050 --> 00:01:34,820
Friendships are a treasure in our life, and everybody should know how to keep their friendships strong and healthy.
